-- UNBUILT (unit SRM17): see REPORT-SRM17.md for run names / exits; the final-SHA rebuild there is the only final evidence.
-- SCOPE (SRM17 audits).  (1) PREMISE TABLE of every new theorem (binders: index, binderInfo, name, Prop-or-data, type) EQUAL to `Tests/Compiler/Srm17AuditExpected.lean` and `scripts/srm17/PREMISES.txt`, one `S17THM` marker per theorem, literal count guard;
-- THREE negative fixtures (semantic ` ∧ True`, added data binder, reordered binders), each non-vacuous and rejected.  REGENERATION: `./.cluster/qbuild.sh build Tests.Compiler.Srm17AuditTest > LOG 2>&1; python3 scripts/srm17/gen_audit.py LOG`.
-- (2) INDEPENDENT EXPECTED STATEMENTS: `Tests/Compiler/Srm17ExpStmt.lean` is GENERATED by scripts/srm17/gen_exp.py from the SRM16 `_viaResetState` SOURCE statements only (explicit deletion list, printed by the script, reading only Tests/Compiler/Srm16ParentTest.lean);
-- each corollary and each residual-fact theorem is `isDefEq` to its expected form; a deliberately wrong form (hfit deleted) is rejected; each residual-fact conclusion is defeq to the SRM16 binder it supplies and NOT defeq to `hrk`/`hsk` (not a relabelling).
-- (3) CLOSURE: standard axioms; forbidden old-form roots (with control); the SRM16 `_viaResetState` theorem is in each corollary's closure, `ran_designP` in each `modP` closure.  NOT guaranteed: that the hypotheses (hsk, FitTree, RegsAtInit, ...) hold for the machine's run.
set_option Elab.async false
set_option autoImplicit false
